/// The brace-list form of the same grant. `import M::{ N }` must offer what
/// `import M;` offers: an `export` grants an importer what the same path would
/// grant if imported there, and naming the item does not narrow that to the
/// module's OWN declarations.
///
/// The static call is the load-bearing assertion, for the reason `main` cannot
/// carry it: a type ANNOTATION resolves through module-level reachability
/// whichever form was written, so it reads the same whether or not the brace
/// list saw the re-export. A static call needs the name bound in SCOPE.
namespace ReexportBasic::Specific;

import ReexportBasic::Aggregate::{ Widget };

function via_specific() -> i32 {
    const w: Widget = Widget::of(6);
    return w.unwrap();
}
